# SafeScribe Database (Prisma + PostgreSQL)

## Multi-Tenant Rules

- `Tenant` (organization) is the isolation boundary.
- Every tenant-owned model includes `tenantId String` + `tenant Tenant @relation(...)`.
- Composite indexes: `@@index([tenantId, createdAt])`, `@@index([tenantId, status])` on list tables.
- Super Admin platform records may omit `tenantId` where appropriate (e.g., platform settings).

## Core Models (Phase 1–3)

`Tenant`, `User`, `Role`, `Permission`, `RolePermission`, `UserRole`, `Session`, `RefreshToken`, `MfaSecret`, `AuditLog`, `LoginHistory`.

User fields: email (unique per tenant or globally — pick one, document it), passwordHash, status (`ACTIVE` | `SUSPENDED` | `PENDING`), failedLoginAttempts, lockedUntil, emailVerifiedAt, lastLoginAt.

## Conventions

```prisma
model User {
  id        String   @id @default(cuid())
  tenantId  String?
  tenant    Tenant?  @relation(fields: [tenantId], references: [id])
  email     String
  createdAt DateTime @default(now())
  updatedAt DateTime @updatedAt

  @@unique([tenantId, email])
  @@index([tenantId, status])
}
```

- IDs: `@default(cuid())` for strings; relations on both sides.
- Timestamps: `createdAt` + `updatedAt` on all entities.
- Soft delete: prefer `deletedAt DateTime?` over hard delete for users/tenants.
- AuditLog: append-only, never update/delete.

## Seeds

Seed script must create: Super Admin (static env credentials), sample tenant, Pharmacist Admin, Pharmacist, default roles/permissions.

## Migrations

One migration per logical change. Run `prisma migrate dev` locally; never edit applied migration SQL.
